[Themes "g5-pawn-storm"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. Nc3 e6 5. Bg5 h6 6. Bh4 dxc4 { Takes the pawn. Black plans to keep it with ...g5 and ...b5. } 7. e4 g5 { Attacks the bishop on h4 and wins space. The h6 pawn guards g5, so White cannot simply take it. }
8. Bg3 ( 8. Nxg5 hxg5 9. Bxg5 Be7 { Black is a knight up for two pawns. The bishop defends the knight on f6, which was attacked from g5. } ) 8... b5 { Supports the extra pawn on c4, so White cannot easily win it back. } 9. Be2 Bb7 { Puts the bishop on the long diagonal, where it presses on e4. } 10. O-O Nbd7 { Finishes development and guards the knight on f6. } *
